; Valuation-commodity fixture (CLEANUP.md HOLD-3), `D`-directive half.
;
; Here BOTH candidate bases price the portfolio, so "the base that prices the
; most holdings" cannot break the tie and frequency alone would answer `EUR`
; (two `… EUR` directives against one `… $`). The journal states which commodity
; it is denominated in — `D $1,000.00` — and that is what settles it.
;
; Deleting the `D` line flips the report to EUR (`marketValue = 1,100.00 EUR`,
; `basis = null`, since no rate converts the `$120.00` cost annotation to EUR),
; which is exactly what the `d_directive_*` tests assert in both directions.
;
; Verified against hledger 1.52:
;   $ hledger -f fixtures/reports/fx-cross-rates-declared.journal bal --value=end,'$' -e 2026-07-16
;     → $1,200.00 assets:broker:vti

D $1,000.00

account assets:broker:vti    ; type: A
account assets:broker:cash   ; type: A
account equity:opening       ; type: E

2026-01-01 opening balance
    assets:broker:cash    $2,000.00
    equity:opening

2026-01-05 buy VTI
    assets:broker:vti     10 VTI @ $120.00
    assets:broker:cash

; VTI is quoted in both commodities, so both can value the position.
P 2026-06-30 VTI $120.00
P 2026-06-30 VTI 110.00 EUR

; One more EUR-targeted rate, enough to outvote `$` on frequency alone.
P 2026-07-01 GBP 1.15 EUR
